# Frontend HTML Practice

This repository contains my HTML learning and practice work. I am learning frontend development step by step and practicing different HTML concepts with practical examples.

## 📌 About This Project

The purpose of this repository is to understand HTML concepts through hands-on practice and improve my frontend development skills.

## 📂 Files Included

### 1. `1_ordered_list.html`
Practice of HTML Ordered Lists.

Topics covered:
- Number List
- Capital Letter List
- Small Letter List
- Roman Capital List
- Roman Small List
- HTML list items

### 2. `2_unordered_list.html`
Practice of HTML Unordered Lists.

### 3. `3_nested_unordered.html`
Practice of Nested Unordered Lists.

### 4. `4_nested_ordered.html`
Practice of Nested Ordered Lists.

## 📚 HTML Concepts Practiced

- HTML Headings (`h1` to `h6`)
- Ordered Lists (`ol`)
- Unordered Lists (`ul`)
- List Items (`li`)
- Ordered List Types
- Nested Lists
- HTML Basic Structure

## 💻 Technologies Used

- HTML5
- Visual Studio Code
- Git
- GitHub

## 🚀 How to Run This Project

1. Clone this repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/namratakinkar/frontend-html-practice.git
   ```

2. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.

3. Select any HTML file.

4. Right-click and select **Open with Live Server** (if installed), or open the HTML file directly in your web browser.

## 🎯 Learning Objectives

- Understand HTML fundamentals.
- Learn different types of HTML lists.
- Practice nested lists.
- Improve frontend development skills.
- Learn Git and GitHub for project management.
- Maintain a collection of practical coding examples.

## 📈 Project Status

Currently learning and practicing HTML concepts. More frontend topics and practical examples will be added as I continue learning.

